<h2>Summary</h2>

GitTorrent is a next-generation version control system (VCS) engineered for extreme performance, decentralized collaboration, and secure automation. It addresses the architectural bottlenecks of legacy systems by combining Content-Defined Chunking (CDC), parallelized hashing, and a Peer-to-Peer (P2P) synchronization model.

By leveraging modern cryptographic primitives and compression algorithms, it provides a significantly more space-efficient and faster alternative for managing large-scale workspaces and remote code execution.

> **Note:** This project is still being developed. As the software grows larger and more powerful, more information will be added.

<h2>Features</h2>

<h3>Content-Defined Chunking</h3>

Utilizes **FastCDC** to optimize workspace snapshots. This method intelligently handles data insertions, deletions, and reordering, reducing space complexity by approximately 10% compared to traditional archiving.

<h3>High-Speed Parallel Hashing</h3>

Powered by **Blake3**, the system handles version identification and file enumeration with native parallel tasking, resulting in calculation speeds ~50x faster than standard SHA-256 implementations.

<h3>Secure Remote Execution</h3>

Features built-in, encrypted remote code execution for CI/CD tasks using **SSH** and **ChaCha20-Poly1305**, ensuring that secrets and automation commands remain protected via password-backed safety.

<h3>P2P Synchronization</h3>

A decentralized Peer-To-Peer network allows users to participate in and stay up-to-date with projects worldwide without relying on a centralized server.

<h2>Technical Implementation</h2>

GitTorrent represents a fundamental redesign of VCS internals to eliminate legacy inefficiencies:

<h3>Merkle Tree Indexing</h3>

Unlike Git’s space-complex indexing, GitTorrent transitions to **Blake3’s native Merkle Tree support**. This creates more efficient enumerations and reduces the space complexity of index files by orders of magnitude.

<h3>Optimized Compression Stack</h3>

The system replaces the aging Zlib "deflate" method with **Zstandard (Zstd)**. This modern algorithm offers faster calculation speeds and better compression ratios for object blobs.

<h3>Data Homogeneity</h3>

To prevent logic desynchronization across the tool, all core data structures and helper functions are encapsulated within a unified **Helper Crate**, ensuring code homogeneity and architectural stability.

<h2>Installation</h2>

<h3>Arch Linux</h3>

Download the compilation script

```bash
git clone https://aur.archlinux.org/gittorrent.git
```

Enter directory
```bash
cd gittorrent
```

Make the package
```bash
makepkg -sfi
```

<h3>Gentoo Linux</h3>

Enable the Guru repository
```bash
sudo emerge -av app-eselect/eselect-repository

sudo eselect repository enable guru

sudo emaint sync -r guru
```

Download and compile the package
```bash
sudo emerge -av dev-vcs/gittorrent
```

<h3>Source</h3>

Download the source code
```bash
git clone https://git.projectgrid.net/gittorrent.git
```

Enter directory
```bash
cd gittorrent
```

Prepare Cargo
```bash
export RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN=stable
```

Build
```bash
export CARGO_TARGET_DIR=target
cargo build --frozen -r --all-features
```

Install
```bash
install -Dm0755 target/release/gittorrent /usr/bin/
install -Dm644 LICENSE /usr/share/licenses/gittorrent/LICENSE
install -Dm644 README.md /usr/share/doc/gittorrent/README.md
```

<h2>Usage</h2>

<h3>Generate and automatically install shell completion scripts</h3>

```bash
gt cpl -a
```

<h3>Initialize a project</h3>

```bash
gt g ~/example
```

<h3>Track workspace state</h3>

```bash
gt a -u
```

<h3>Duplicate an existing workspace</h3>

```bash
gt d /usr/local/games/example
```

<h3>Save workspace state</h3>

```bash
gt s -m "initial commit"

```

